  "term": "Dexedrine",
  "definition": "Dexedrine is a stimulant drug form of dextroamphetamine that increases brain chemicals such as noradrenaline and dopamine, which can raise alertness, activity, and appetite suppression. It has dependence risk and can increase heart rate and blood pressure, and it is used for narcolepsy and attention deficit hyperactivity disorder.",
